  "tibetan_transliteration": "\u0f60\u0f51\u0f74\u0f63\u0f0b\u0f56\u0f0b\u0f58\u0f51\u0f7c\u0f60\u0f72\u0f0b\u0f51\u0f42\u0f7c\u0f66\u0f0b\u0f60\u0f56\u0fb2\u0f7a\u0f63",
  "comments": "This untitled and anonymous text (possibly incomplete) essentially discusses the \"purpose and connection\" (dgos 'brel) of a treatise (hence the editorial title). It is only on fol. 5a in (ID:5275) that it reveals itself to be about monastic discipline, identifying the topic of the treatise as \"chos 'di pa dag gi tshul khrims.\" The treatise under consideration is likely the Vinayas\u016btra (ID:6821), which has the expression \"tshul khrims\" in its initial verse. The text makes several references to Dharmamitra, the author of the Vinayas\u016btra\u1e6d\u012bk\u0101 (ID:8404).\r\n\r\nThe frequent use of thal...phyir arguments and reference to the Pram\u0101\u1e47av\u0101rttika (ID:3772) suggest a date of composition in the 13th c. or beyond.\r\nThe discussion of dgos 'brel has close parallels to the one found in the Tik chen lung don rnam gzigs (ID:5870) by Chu mig pa Seng ge dpal (ID:4018).",
